<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimated Tuesday 100,000 -USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimated Tuesday 100,000 -USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimated interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog receipts Tuesday were 100,000 head, compared with 115,000 a week ago and 101,000 a year ago.</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts were $1.00 lower than mid-session Monday. Trade and demand light to moderate. Offerings moderate.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    55.50 -56.50	   56.50 -57.50</p>
<p>few			55.00  57.00	   56.00  58.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    54.50 -56.50	   55.00 -57.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    54.50 -56.50	   55.00 -57.50</p>
<p>Sows:  steady to $2.00 higher. US 1-3 300-500 lbs.  43.00 -46.00	   45.00 -47.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    46.00 -48.00	   47.00 -50.00</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
</text>
